# Package files are stored as ordinary git objects, not Git LFS.
#
# Upstream droidian tracks *.deb through LFS. That does not work for a public
# community fork on a free GitHub account: the LFS bandwidth quota is 1 GB per
# month, every clone pulls ~66 MB of packages, and once the quota is gone
# cloning fails for everyone until it resets.
#
# The largest package here is ~47 MB, comfortably under GitHub's 100 MB
# per-file limit, so plain git objects work and clone bandwidth is unmetered.
*.deb !text !filter !merge !diff
